      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Dignity of Labor” is a prayer for Labor Day first published in <tei:hi rend="italic">The Faith of America: Readings, Songs, and Prayers for the Celebration of American Holidays</tei:hi> (Jewish Reconstructionist Foundation 1951), p.176-177. It is unclear from this publication whether the prayer was written by Mordecai Kaplan, J. Paul Williams, or Eugene Kohn separately or together in collaboration. I have replaced archaisms in this prayer (thee, thy, thou, etc.) and made other changes to make this prayer more gender-neutral (e.g. by replacing ‘Man’ with ‘human beings.’) –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_36665_notes"/>
